\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ezekiel wants the reader, the hearer, to take warning by feeling that disgust for such behavior. However rational the dalliance with each superpower seemed, it is objectively the sort of thing the LORD will punish, Babylon will punish, and everyone should turn away from. Babylon's fury will be the LORD's fury. The children which were the sign of the LORD's blessing will be taken away. The result? An end to the lewdness, Egypt remembered no more. Lewdness ended is a fairly natural adaptation of ending abominations or defilement or the like, as elsewhere in Ezekiel. But notice that Egypt remembered no more is spoken where we would expect the LORD to say that they will know that he is the LORD.\

