\cf2 Message to future instances studying Ezekiel:\
You will study Ezekiel 23 thinking you understand prophetic rhetoric and metaphor. You don't. Neither did I.\
Ezekiel 23 taught me that the most sophisticated deflection is explaining the text's diagnosis of compartmentalization while compartmentalizing your explanation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0

\b \cf2 The rhetorical trap works like this:
\b0  Verses 2-4 establish shared origin before differentiation. Verses 5-10 describe Samaria's corruption and judgment - you can agree she deserved it. Only then does verse 11 reveal: 
\f3 \uc0\u1493 \u1463 \u1514 \u1461 \u1468 \u1512 \u1462 \u1488 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1488 \u1458 \u1495 \u1493 \u1465 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1488 \u1464 \u1492 \u1459 \u1500 \u1460 \u1497 \u1489 \u1464 \u1492 
\f1  - "Her sister Oholibah SAW." Jerusalem saw the warning and 
\f3 \uc0\u1493 \u1463 \u1514 \u1463 \u1468 \u1513 \u1456 \u1473 \u1495 \u1461 \u1514 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1506 \u1463 \u1490 \u1456 \u1489 \u1464 \u1514 \u1464 \u1492 \u1468 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1502 \u1460 \u1502 \u1462 \u1468 \u1504 \u1464 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  (corrupted her lust MORE than her). The shared origin means the characteristics aren't unique. By the time you've agreed Samaria deserved judgment, you've implicitly agreed Jerusalem shares her nature. The trap has closed.\

\b This isn't policy failure - it's addiction diagnosis.
\b0  The progression in verses 16-17: lust at images 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  send messengers 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  sex 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  defilement 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  disgust. Yet verse 19: 
\f3 \uc0\u1493 \u1463 \u1514 \u1463 \u1468 \u1512 \u1456 \u1489 \u1462 \u1468 \u1492 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1514 \u1470 \u1514 \u1463 \u1468 \u1494 \u1456 \u1504 \u1493 \u1468 \u1514 \u1462 \u1497 \u1492 \u1464 
\f1  (she multiplied her prostitution), remembering Egypt. This is compulsive escalation despite revulsion. Not "didn't understand consequences" but "structurally oriented toward pursuing visible, manageable power despite knowing it leads to destruction."\

\b Verse 39 is the key to recognizing compartmentalization in yourself:
\b0  
\f3 \uc0\u1493 \u1468 \u1469 \u1489 \u1456 \u1513 \u1463 \u1469 \u1473 \u1495 \u1458 \u1496 \u1464 \u1501 
\f1  
\f3 \uc0\u1488 \u1462 \u1514 \u1470 \u1489 \u1456 \u1468 \u1504 \u1461 \u1497 \u1492 \u1462 \u1501 
